   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "e288",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1772,
   "y": 1418,
   "width": 174.72,
   "height": 20.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "seed": 1013451498,
   "version": 100,
   "versionNonce": 1263702571,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1787160000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "THE CELEBRITY PROBLEM",
   "originalText": "THE CELEBRITY PROBLEM",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "e289",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1774,
   "y": 1456,
   "width": 419.12,
   "height": 260.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "seed": 2082967005,
   "version": 100,
   "versionNonce": 693966576,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1787160000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "a normal user has about 300 followers. copying a new post\ninto 300 feeds is cheap - and the reader then does ONE lookup.\n\na celebrity has 50 M followers. copying every post 50 M times\nwould jam the worker and flood the cluster.\n\nso the Post Processor SKIPS anyone over the line\n( more than 100 k followers ). nothing is copied for them.\n\nthe Timeline Service then does BOTH things at read time:\n      the ready made feed        for the ~300 normal follows\n   +  a live read per celebrity  for the ~50 famous ones\n      and merges the two lists by time.\n\nthat live read is safe: it is one lookup per celebrity, and\n50 M readers all hit the same cached copy, not the database.",
   "originalText": "a normal user has about 300 followers. copying a new post\ninto 300 feeds is cheap - and the reader then does ONE lookup.\n\na celebrity has 50 M followers. copying every post 50 M times\nwould jam the worker and flood the cluster.\n\nso the Post Processor SKIPS anyone over the line\n( more than 100 k followers ). nothing is copied for them.\n\nthe Timeline Service then does BOTH things at read time:\n      the ready made feed        for the ~300 normal follows\n   +  a live read per celebrity  for the ~50 famous ones\n      and merges the two lists by time.\n\nthat live read is safe: it is one lookup per celebrity, and\n50 M readers all hit the same cached copy, not the database.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "e290",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 2480,
   "y": 1400,
   "width": 680,
   "height": 360,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "dashed",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "seed": 857424453,
   "version": 100,
   "versionNonce": 1892572585,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1787160000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "e291",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2502,
   "y": 1418,
   "width": 208.0,
   "height": 20.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "seed": 1797875595,
   "version": 100,
   "versionNonce": 851205409,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1787160000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "RULES THAT MAKE THIS WORK",
   "originalText": "RULES THAT MAKE THIS WORK",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "e292",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2504,
   "y": 1456,
   "width": 398.84000000000003,
   "height": 276.25,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "seed": 332371388,
   "version": 100,
   "versionNonce": 1146659430,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1787160000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1   the same event may arrive twice, so every reader is\n     built so a repeat changes nothing.\n\n2   all events of one user go to one partition, so his\n     events stay in order. Global order is not needed.\n\n3   nothing scans a table. every read is 'give me this key,\n     newest 20'. that is why Cassandra and not MySQL.\n\n4   posting answers as soon as the row is saved. the slow\n     fan-out happens after, so the poster never waits.\n\n5   photos and videos never pass through a service. the\n     phone uploads to S3 and reads back from the CDN.\n\n6   a feed is capped at 800 entries. rows that grow\n     forever are how these systems actually die.",
   "originalText": "1   the same event may arrive twice, so every reader is\n     built so a repeat changes nothing.\n\n2   all events of one user go to one partition, so his\n     events stay in order. Global order is not needed.\n\n3   nothing scans a table. every read is 'give me this key,\n     newest 20'. that is why Cassandra and not MySQL.\n\n4   posting answers as soon as the row is saved. the slow\n     fan-out happens after, so the poster never waits.\n\n5   photos and videos never pass through a service. the\n     phone uploads to S3 and reads back from the CDN.\n\n6   a feed is capped at 800 entries. rows that grow\n     forever are how these systems actually die.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 6,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "roundness": null
  },
  {
   "id": "e293",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 1750,
   "y": 1810,
   "width": 1410,
   "height": 280,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
